WEBVTT

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:44.010
Mr. Fairy's through here, right?

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:46.440
Hey!

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:47.780
SARG 5.

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:49.700
Yes, this is SARG 5.

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:51.410
Awaiting your report.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:53.350
Arrived without incident...

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:56.340
...at Morgue.

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:57.700
Understood.

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:02.370
And what about the alien you encountered?

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:06.030
It was just like a SARG, no question about it.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:09.600
The same design, size, mobility, power...

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:13.740
No, except it was maybe
a little better than mine.

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:17.040
Can you send the battle log?

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:19.410
Yes, I'll encrypt and send it.

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:21.750
We'll work on the analysis.

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:24.310
Meanwhile, continue as instructed.

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:25.650
Roger.

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:28.210
What are you thinking?

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:30.820
Do you think you could leave this one to me?

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:31.880
Oh?

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:33.830
There's something bothering me.

00:02:36.070 --> 00:02:37.230
Very well.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:38.430
It's yours.

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:49.390
Welcome to Morgue.

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:51.270
Maki?

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:54.980
Hattie...

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:03.120
What is this facility?

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:05.090
You must have heard.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:07.030
About half a year ago...

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:11.160
Some crazy researchers did
unauthorized experiments and...

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:17.100
It cost nearly a year's funding
to put this place back together.

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:26.640
How much longer till we see Mr. Fairy?

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:39.690
Surprising maneuverability.

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:56.910
Is it coincidence or fate?

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:03.910
It's me.

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:06.810
I see.

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:08.120
Mistel, you say?

00:04:09.130 --> 00:04:10.290
That's too bad.

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:12.760
I was hoping we'd have it fixed sooner.

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:14.960
Hold on.

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:16.520
Page Lt. Harris.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:18.790
I want to discuss test runs.

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:28.640
We should run a check on pattern B-16 first.

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:31.840
I still say D-22's the priority.

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:34.440
No, according to previous data...

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:36.340
Please, professors.

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:38.680
We don't need an argument.

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:41.840
We need to revive this monster first.

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:45.050
Make him a more efficient
weapon than before.

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:46.620
Understood...

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:49.570
Let's go with F-6.

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:51.630
No, we haven't tested them.

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:53.600
I'd be okay with that.

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:55.100
But we can't...

00:04:57.580 --> 00:04:59.810
V-Very well.

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:01.610
I suppose it's all right.

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:04.770
Then let's get to it.

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:06.240
Y-Yes, sir.

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:07.080
Very well.

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:10.150
The scientists are a pain in my side.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:13.120
Morgue is a fitting name.

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:16.520
They're like hyenas playing among corpses.

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:19.930
They'll do anything for military money.

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:23.550
Scientists...

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:27.170
I used to think they had some kind of code...

00:05:27.170 --> 00:05:30.100
...but now I know that
we soldiers are the true idealists.

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:31.430
You know?

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:34.770
Some scientists still believe in ideals.

00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:37.150
Excuse me.

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:39.310
My work makes a body tired.

00:05:58.700 --> 00:05:59.930
Mr. Fairy?

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:04.230
This is where he was born, right?

00:06:05.810 --> 00:06:10.250
Everybody's waiting for Mr. Fairy to wake up.

00:06:10.310 --> 00:06:13.390
All that effort just made you sleepy, right?

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:17.680
Hurry and wake up so we can go play.

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:19.690
That's not likely.

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:21.690
He'll never wake up.

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:24.000
He's dead.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:25.030
He can't...

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:27.460
Just like your parents and grandfather.

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:30.730
Dead people don't come back.

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:33.490
I said it before.

00:06:33.570 --> 00:06:35.970
It's the same as the land of the fairies.

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:38.170
You have to live in the real world.

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:41.800
It's called "Neverland"
because you'll never find it.

00:06:45.650 --> 00:06:46.810
Don't shut up.

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:50.720
I don't know what you're
thinking if you shut up.

00:06:51.490 --> 00:06:52.680
Stupid!

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:56.320
Ryu Soma is stupid!

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:03.280
December 31st?

00:07:03.330 --> 00:07:05.780
Right, New Year's Eve.

00:07:06.170 --> 00:07:08.470
He brought me home...

00:07:08.470 --> 00:07:13.240
...and then kept pleading with
me to go out with him for hours.

00:07:13.310 --> 00:07:14.300
And then?

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:18.010
I heard "Happy New Year" and firecrackers...

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:22.920
...and realized it was a new year
and somehow felt I could do it.

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:27.930
That's how you hooked up
with your first boyfriend?

00:07:28.690 --> 00:07:30.290
Is it funny?

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:32.300
Sure, it's funny.

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:34.630
Because it was a new year?

00:07:34.700 --> 00:07:35.760
That's the reason?

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:43.780
So what happened?

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:45.910
You like talking about this?

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:47.120
Yeah.

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:48.410
But...

00:07:48.410 --> 00:07:50.410
I want to know you.

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:56.180
About your old boyfriends,
about when you were a kid...

00:07:56.250 --> 00:07:59.310
What you like and your experiences.

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:01.820
Is that weird?

00:08:04.600 --> 00:08:05.510
Stupid...

00:08:09.770 --> 00:08:10.520
Stupid!

00:08:24.250 --> 00:08:26.030
We're getting ready to start.

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:30.090
You know the background?

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:31.780
Not really.

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:33.820
I don't know much myself.

00:08:33.890 --> 00:08:36.090
But when they revived it the first time,

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:38.960
it seems that they input some kind of program.

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:40.200
Program?

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:43.870
Designed by a female student
working with the professor...

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:47.300
No one really knows any more details.

00:08:51.240 --> 00:08:54.970
Anyway, this is what our
wonderful scientists came up with.

00:08:58.820 --> 00:08:59.820
Those are...

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:03.280
A way to get what we want.

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:42.860
Only four have any
chance of proving useful.

00:09:42.990 --> 00:09:47.520
The only way to disable
an alien is through the neck.

00:09:47.590 --> 00:09:50.970
Aren't they mistaking them
for zombies and vampires?

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:55.630
Excuse me.

00:09:57.070 --> 00:09:58.340
It's you.

00:09:58.410 --> 00:09:59.570
What is it?

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:00.880
Explain this procedure.

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:03.740
Pointless. You wouldn't understand.

00:10:03.810 --> 00:10:06.430
You realize I'm here as
a representative of Funeral.

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:10.010
Well, in that case...

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:17.460
A 3D pulse electricity circuit
brain network controls the aliens.

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:20.990
Their sense of judgment
comes from this system.

00:10:20.990 --> 00:10:25.970
However, we've found the EX-1
is deficient in this system.

00:10:25.970 --> 00:10:30.030
So we're trying to copy
over the missing patterns...

00:10:30.110 --> 00:10:32.160
...to rebuild the EX-1.

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:33.820
It won't work.

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:34.700
Why is that?

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:35.800
Frank...

00:10:35.880 --> 00:10:40.520
No, the EX-1 has a backlog of experiences.

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:45.120
If you rewrite those memories
with the aliens' thought patterns...

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:47.600
"Memories"?

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:49.560
And "thought patterns"?

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:54.590
That's just a heap of iron out there.

00:10:54.870 --> 00:10:58.440
It doesn't have "memories"
or anything close to that.

00:10:58.770 --> 00:11:01.770
It's just recorded data.

00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:06.670
It sounds like you're mistaking
him for something human.

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:09.160
Don't be silly.

00:11:12.820 --> 00:11:16.580
Pursuit, curiosity, drive!

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:19.920
Lack even one and you'll never find the truth!

00:11:21.090 --> 00:11:25.510
How can everyone be satisfied
with the same, tired answers?

00:11:25.730 --> 00:11:29.220
Are there no students of
knowledge at this college?

00:11:29.470 --> 00:11:30.900
The Old Testament!

00:11:30.970 --> 00:11:35.270
They didn't stop searching even though
it meant repeated punishment!

00:11:36.370 --> 00:11:39.100
It's an abundant sea of imagination.

00:11:39.180 --> 00:11:42.110
And we are all ships on that sea.

00:11:42.280 --> 00:11:44.410
Be devoutly curious!

00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:46.710
If you want to move forward!

00:11:53.260 --> 00:11:54.990
You guys aren't...

00:11:54.990 --> 00:11:56.000
...moving forward.

00:11:56.460 --> 00:11:58.220
Did you say something?

00:11:58.300 --> 00:12:02.490
No, at this rate, you'll advance
one-tenth of a percent.

00:12:29.230 --> 00:12:31.920
All personnel, report final status!

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:45.720
We're on duty.

00:12:46.140 --> 00:12:47.840
Don't worry about it.

00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:49.720
Engine power good.

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:51.920
It's stable at high speed.

00:12:51.980 --> 00:12:53.780
Better than before.

00:12:54.220 --> 00:12:57.690
Then let's try a short-distance
takeoff and landing.

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:00.650
Head for Riverfield Base.

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:01.820
But that's...

00:13:01.890 --> 00:13:04.260
Don't you want to surprise Harriet?

00:13:06.110 --> 00:13:07.590
Aye, aye, sir!

00:13:20.710 --> 00:13:24.300
Designed by a female student
working with the professor...

00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:29.150
Maki...

00:13:32.920 --> 00:13:34.220
What did you...

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:37.220
...talk to him about?

00:13:53.410 --> 00:13:54.810
Hidden files?

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:56.940
A bug?

00:14:17.130 --> 00:14:19.030
Th-This is...

00:14:21.970 --> 00:14:23.070
No!

00:14:26.480 --> 00:14:28.140
Commence contact!

00:14:44.600 --> 00:14:48.760
3D brain circuit network in
the sample heads confirmed.

00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:51.480
Stop the experiment!

00:14:51.480 --> 00:14:53.330
What do you think you're doing?

00:14:59.640 --> 00:15:00.740
Th-This is...

00:15:01.110 --> 00:15:03.240
They're rebuilding themselves!

00:15:03.240 --> 00:15:05.050
There was such a program?

00:15:05.120 --> 00:15:06.200
There was.

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:08.660
It was all part of the input.

00:15:10.920 --> 00:15:13.320
But they don't have alien motors.

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:16.020
The bodies are just shells.

00:15:17.690 --> 00:15:20.920
You won't see it if you're looking
for the same, tired answers.

00:15:22.470 --> 00:15:23.760
A problem at Morgue?

00:15:24.070 --> 00:15:26.050
It apparently just happened.

00:15:26.420 --> 00:15:27.700
I knew it...

00:15:27.770 --> 00:15:28.980
What, Captain?

00:15:28.980 --> 00:15:30.810
I'll tell you when I get back.

00:15:30.810 --> 00:15:32.730
We should assist them.

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:34.450
Permission granted. Move in.

00:15:34.630 --> 00:15:35.650
Roger.

00:15:36.110 --> 00:15:37.770
Lt. Harris, full power.

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:40.110
Jeez, this is some practice run.

00:15:45.690 --> 00:15:46.820
E-Evacuate!

00:15:46.890 --> 00:15:48.220
Evacuate!

00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:54.090
Evacuate!

00:15:54.090 --> 00:15:55.150
Wait!

00:15:55.230 --> 00:15:56.930
You're going to leave Frank?

00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:59.420
Don't be stupid! It's a hunk of metal!

00:15:59.420 --> 00:16:01.060
And you call yourself...

00:16:04.340 --> 00:16:05.330
Hattie!

00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:12.740
Wait there!

00:16:16.920 --> 00:16:18.230
Can you hear me, Hattie?

00:16:21.590 --> 00:16:23.670
An emergency hatch is behind you!

00:16:23.670 --> 00:16:24.690
No!

00:16:24.760 --> 00:16:25.910
What are you saying?

00:16:25.910 --> 00:16:29.370
We can't leave Mr. Fairy!

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:30.800
You'll die!

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:33.060
I won't go!

00:16:33.140 --> 00:16:36.230
He's saved my life lots of times!

00:16:36.310 --> 00:16:39.250
This time, I have to save him.

00:16:39.480 --> 00:16:41.000
Don't be stupid!

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:42.300
I'm not stupid!

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:47.010
Stupid...

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:57.920
Please...

00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:00.660
Not in front of me again like this...

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:15.030
You...

00:17:19.750 --> 00:17:21.680
Why are you lying there?

00:17:37.870 --> 00:17:39.730
She shouldn't be killed...

00:17:40.800 --> 00:17:41.740
It should be you!

00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:49.540
You see.

00:17:49.610 --> 00:17:51.080
Everything's just like it was before.

00:17:53.150 --> 00:17:55.810
Morgue, me, and you!

00:17:56.690 --> 00:17:59.160
Only this time, no professor or Maki.

00:18:03.390 --> 00:18:04.550
That's rich.

00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:07.830
Like a cheap soap opera.

00:18:10.770 --> 00:18:15.170
So wake up like a cheap superhero!

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:17.970
And wake up again and again!

00:18:18.040 --> 00:18:19.510
And die!

00:18:19.580 --> 00:18:23.610
That should be your punishment
for taking Maki away from me!

00:18:42.630 --> 00:18:44.160
I...

00:18:45.340 --> 00:18:48.060
...want to...

00:18:48.540 --> 00:18:52.300
...know more about you.

00:18:55.910 --> 00:18:56.970
Maki.

00:19:06.720 --> 00:19:33.780
Hattie!

00:19:36.920 --> 00:19:38.790
Maki!

00:19:42.760 --> 00:19:43.750
Stop!

00:19:54.270 --> 00:19:55.430
Mr. Fairy!

00:20:01.040 --> 00:20:02.880
Frank...

00:20:02.950 --> 00:20:04.010
You...

00:20:25.800 --> 00:20:26.960
Mr. Fairy!

00:20:29.670 --> 00:20:31.400
Welcome back!

00:20:31.480 --> 00:20:34.310
Welcome back, Mr. Fairy.

00:20:46.320 --> 00:20:47.480
Thank you!

00:20:48.490 --> 00:20:50.650
You woke him up!

00:20:50.650 --> 00:20:51.920
Thank you, Ryu!

00:20:59.070 --> 00:21:00.090
I...

00:21:03.540 --> 00:21:04.740
In Neverland...

00:21:05.810 --> 00:21:08.840
Fairies are born whenever children laugh,

00:21:08.840 --> 00:21:13.110
but they die when children stop believing.

00:21:13.180 --> 00:21:15.480
I know that! From Peter Pan.

00:21:17.190 --> 00:21:19.920
It wasn't me who woke him up.

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:22.250
Perhaps...

00:21:31.000 --> 00:21:33.060
Rising from the graveyard, huh?

00:21:39.210 --> 00:21:41.770
This is the second time it's happened.

00:21:41.850 --> 00:21:45.490
There is no coincidence
without inevitability in this world.

00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:51.610
I want...

00:21:52.760 --> 00:21:54.280
...to know more...

00:21:56.290 --> 00:21:57.620
...about...

00:21:58.630 --> 00:21:59.650
...myself.

00:22:00.660 --> 00:22:01.860
This is...

00:22:02.870 --> 00:22:04.530
What?

00:22:04.530 --> 00:22:05.550
Who?

00:22:22.250 --> 00:22:23.580
I want...

00:22:24.590 --> 00:22:29.320
...to know more about you, too.

00:22:35.930 --> 00:22:37.750
The past has left the stage.

00:22:38.470 --> 00:22:40.700
Cast away from Heaven and Earth.

00:22:41.370 --> 00:22:44.270
The final tale, rich with poison.

00:22:45.540 --> 00:22:48.600
Next time,
Answers and the Past.
